    "provenance": "original",
    "title": {
     "en": "How many are left?"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "A driver carries 700 sacks of rice and delivers 250. How many are left?"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "subtract",
     "take away",
     "regroup",
     "difference"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "To subtract, take away the ones, then the tens, then the hundreds.\nThink of 700 - 250. 700 is 7 hundreds. Take away 2 hundreds to get 500, then take away 5 tens to get 450.\nIf there are not enough ones, break one ten into ten ones. This is called regrouping.\nThe difference is the answer of a subtraction. It tells how much more or how much less.\nUse a number line to count back or count up. From 250 count up to 700 to find the difference.\nCheck subtraction by adding: 450 + 250 should be 700."
    }
   },
